extraction_notes: "Page span: the Psi-Net section opens on printed 190; the class heading PRP/Psi-Net Agent is at the foot of printed 193, the unit roster, attributes, bonuses, Investigation, the two optional MOS packages and the first O.C.C. skills fill printed 194, and the rest of the entry fills printed 195. Printed 196 is a full-page illustration. GROUP: psychic. The section is the Coalition''s psychic regulatory and police branch and three quarters of its agents are psychics, so men_of_arms false. RACE: see race_restrictions. PSIONICS: the book prints no psionic powers, tier or I.S.P. for the class, only the unit''s mix; no psionics block is stored, so a human agent rolls for psionics in the ordinary way. Not stored as a tier because the book does not fix one. INVESTIGATION: a special skill with no catalog row, stored as a special ability rather than as a stub skill. MOS: four +15% skills from one of eight areas, or the Tracker or Spotter package in their place, modelled as skills.mos with ten options. The book''s Electronics is the Electrical category and Piloting is Pilot. The packages'' non-skill bonuses (Tracker +1 vs horror factor and +5% Investigation; Spotter +1 initiative) cannot ride on an MOS option and are special abilities. Track Animals is stored as Track & Trap Animals, Track (humanoids) as Tracking (people). The Spotter''s Lore of choice offers the catalog''s Rifts lore rows. O.C.C. SKILLS: the entry prints no language line, so none is stored. HAND TO HAND: Expert, changeable to Martial Arts or Assassin (evil) for two related skills. BONUSES: +1 vs psionic attack and mind control, +2 vs magic illusion, +1 vs possession, +1 vs horror factor at 1, 4, 8, 12 and 15. MONEY: 2D6x1000 credits to start, confirmed from a render because the text layer ciphers it; salary is prose. ARMOR: new style Dead Boy armor is CA-3 light or CA-4 standard, or street clothes. E-clips: four for each weapon, stored as eight. The flares are stored as signal flares, the flash grenades as stun/flash grenades, the tear gas grenades as the Tear Gas Grenade row, the silver plated survival knife as the silver plated knife and the silver cross as the small silver cross. Vehicles are prose; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3."
